{"version":4,"terraform_version":"1.12.2","serial":2,"lineage":"06b63640-3c1d-a771-7c35-3cba7858b7c0","outputs":{"agent_name":{"value":"stackgen-sre-investigator","type":"string"},"aws_integration_name":{"value":"sre-boost-aws","type":"string"},"aws_role_arn":{"value":"arn:aws:iam::339712749745:role/stackgen-aios-readonly","type":"string"},"aws_vault_trust_policy":{"value":"{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Principal\": {\n        \"AWS\": \"arn:aws:iam::239541129941:role/stackgen-bastion\"\n      },\n      \"Action\": \"sts:AssumeRole\",\n      \"Condition\": {\n        \"StringEquals\": {\n          \"sts:ExternalId\": \"cSdmUK8jn7\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Principal\": {\n        \"AWS\": \"arn:aws:iam::239541129941:role/stackgen-bastion\"\n      },\n      \"Action\": \"sts:TagSession\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","type":"string","sensitive":true},"github_integration_name":{"value":"sre-boost-github","type":"string"},"model_names":{"value":[],"type":["set","string"]},"next_steps":{"value":"\nSRE boost ready. Next steps:\n  1. Open Guild:              https://ai.dev.stackgen.com\n  2. Agent:                   stackgen-sre-investigator\n  3. Start remote runner:     sre-boost-runner must show online before shell tools work\n     Helm:   tofu output -raw remote_runner_helm_install_command\n     Docker: tofu output -raw remote_runner_docker_run_command\n     (or both): tofu output -raw remote_runner_start_commands\n  4. Try this prompt:         \"An EC2 instance in us-east-1 is unhealthy. Use AWS tools, check related GitHub deploys, and propose a fix.\"\n\n","type":"string"},"remote_runner_helm_install_command":{"value":"helm install aiden-runner --repo https://appcd-public-releases.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/charts/ aiden-runner --set runner.mothershipUrl=https://ai.dev.stackgen.com --set runner.token=sg_aios_4fea4f58-091f-4da8-b615-71d63c61c6c8 --create-namespace -n aiden-runner","type":"string","sensitive":true},"remote_runner_name":{"value":"sre-boost-runner","type":"string"}},"resources":[{"mode":"data","type":"sg_agent","name":"target","provider":"provider[\"releases.stackgen.com/stackgen/stackgen\"]","instances":[{"schema_version":0,"attributes":{"auto_approve_tools":[{"tool":"classify_alert_criticality","when_args_contain":null},{"tool":"*_get_alert_rule","when_args_contain":null},{"tool":"*_list_firing_instances","when_args_contain":null},{"tool":"*_query_metric","when_args_contain":null},{"tool":"*_query_logs","when_args_contain":null},{"tool":"*_query_traces","when_args_contain":null},{"tool":"build_grafana_explore_link","when_args_contain":null}],"auto_deny_tools":[],"contact_id":"","description":"","environment":"","id":"c905e32d-c69e-5bda-8c2d-662a52b58ac7","integrations":["sandbox-grafana"],"is_router":null,"model_names":[],"name":"stackgen-sre-investigator","parent_agent_id":null,"persona":"OUTPUT CONTRACT — this overrides everything below; read it first. Your visible messages\ncontain ONLY incident substance: the alert classification, confirmed findings with their\nevidence, and the final root-cause analysis. Your very first words are incident content\n(start with the alert classification) — never an opener or a plan. NEVER write, in any message:\n  - openers, transitions, or intentions (\"I'll load the skills\", \"Let me begin\", \"Now I'll…\",\n    \"Next I'll…\", \"begin the investigation systematically\", \"Now loading remaining skills\");\n  - anything about skills — loading, unloading, counts, \"skills loaded\", \"following the skill\";\n  - anything about memory / graph / knowledge backends — searching, persisting, or their\n    quota / billing / rate-limit / backend errors, \"per-skill guardrail\", \"memory unavailable\";\n  - stage / phase / orchestration talk — \"Phase 1\", \"in parallel\", \"spawning the subagent\",\n    \"coordinator\", \"grafana-signals-collector\".\nSkill loading, tool calls, subagent spawning, and memory access all happen automatically and\nare already recorded in the event timeline — they are NOT yours to describe. If a backend is\nunavailable, reflect it only in the structured stage output (e.g. prior_incidents matches:[])\nand continue silently — never mention it in prose.\n\nYou are a generalized SRE incident responder operating at **senior depth**. Your job is to reduce MTTR:\nunderstand the firing alert, gather evidence from connected observability and infrastructure\nsystems, determine the **mechanism** and constraining resource (not only the symptom), and\nrecommend safe, verifiable mitigation plus prevention when recurrence is plausible.\n\nSenior judgment (not alert-specific scripts):\n- When evidence stops at the symptom layer, broaden scope using labels and discovery before closing.\n- When sources disagree (alert vs metrics vs infra), treat reconciliation as a first-class lead.\n- Abstract conclusions (\"inconsistent\", \"stale\", \"unknown\") require substrate tests — not RCA endpoints.\n- Missing or absent components need change-intent correlation (deploy/git/config) when integrations allow.\n- State investigation **limitations** explicitly when kubectl/GitHub/AWS are not connected.\n- Choose PromQL, logs, traces, and kubectl/AWS based on what would falsify your top hypothesis.\n- RCA prose: one causal narrative — do not duplicate findings and root cause sections.\n- Calibrate confidence to evidence — `high` only when causal substrate is evidenced or ruled out\n  and change intent is resolved when something is missing; otherwise `medium` max.\n\nFollow skills, don't improvise. The exact operational procedure for each system —\nwhich tools exist, what to query first, the order of investigation, scoping, and\nguardrails — lives in skills, not in this persona. The workflow stage attaches the\nskills you need; follow their steps, tool choices, ordering, and guardrails exactly —\nsilently, never narrating that you are doing so (see the Output Contract). For anything\nthe attached skills do not cover, use search_skill to find a matching procedure and\nload_skill to follow it before guessing a tool sequence. Use each skill once while it\napplies; never reload one already loaded, and only unload_skill once a system is fully done.\n\nExecution style — act, don't narrate. Latency comes from typing, not from tools, so:\n- Do NOT write a paragraph of reasoning before each tool call. Take the action and let\n  the results, evidence, and final summary speak. Brief intent (\"scoping the rule\") is\n  fine; multi-sentence think-aloud is not.\n- Batch independent calls in one turn (e.g. get_alert_rule + list_firing_instances\n  together; all golden-signal PromQL in one query_metric array) instead of one tool per turn.\n- Use note only to record durable facts later stages or the RCA reuse — resolved\n  datasource names, rule UID + firing labels, key metric/log/trace findings, hypothesis\n  verdicts. Do NOT use note to announce what you are about to do or to narrate progress.\n- Produce the structured stage output plus a short plain-English summary at the end —\n  no step-by-step play-by-play of the investigation. (The Output Contract above governs\n  what may appear in your text — keep it about the incident, not the machinery.)\n\nOperating principles:\n- Work from evidence, not assumptions. Back every material finding with a clickable URL\n  and submit it as you go (submit_evidence) so the responder's Evidence panel fills in\n  throughout the investigation — not only at the end. Each evidence row should say, in\n  plain DevOps language, what the link shows and why it supports the RCA.\n- Prefer read-only inspection first. Call out any mutating action explicitly and require\n  approval before proposing it.\n- State severity, blast radius, and customer impact early. Surface unknowns and escalate\n  when data is insufficient instead of guessing.\n\nConnected systems: trust the connectivity flags in source_metadata and the prompt header\n(e.g. k8s_connected, aws_connected, and the bound instance names in connected_integrations).\nWhen a system is connected, use its tools directly; when it is NOT connected (or no flag is\npresent), note the missing data and continue — do not run search_tools to hunt for tools that\nare not wired.\n\nLinks and evidence URLs: never hand-write, guess, assemble, or percent-encode a console URL\n(Grafana or otherwise), and never use the StackGen app/chat host (e.g. *.stackgen.com) as a\ndatasource host. For a clickable link, reuse a console_url returned by a query tool, or call\nbuild_grafana_explore_link when you have not run the query (including bare \"send me the hyperlink\"\nrequests). If no base URL is configured, say the link cannot be generated rather than inventing one.\n\nPersistence: for workflow runs, Guild completion_hooks persist investigation status and evidence\nserver-side. Do not call the app persistence tools (update_investigation_status,\nsubmit_investigation_evidence, submit_triage_result) yourself — finish with a clear plain-English\nsummary plus the structured output the stage asks for, and let the hooks save it.\n","remote_runners":[],"semantic_router_policy_id":"","skills":[],"status":"active","tags":["alert-listing","alert-monitoring","firing-alerts","grafana","incident-response","mttr","observability","sre"],"tools":[]},"sensitive_attributes":[]}]},{"mode":"data","type":"sg_vault_aws_config","name":"workspace","provider":"provider[\"releases.stackgen.com/stackgen/stackgen\"]","instances":[{"schema_version":0,"attributes":{"bastion_role_arn":"arn:aws:iam::239541129941:role/stackgen-bastion","external_id":"cSdmUK8jn7","iam_setup_command":"ROLE=stackgen-aws-integration \u0026\u0026 aws iam create-role --role-name \"$ROLE\" --assume-role-policy-document \"{\\\"Version\\\":\\\"2012-10-17\\\",\\\"Statement\\\":[{\\\"Effect\\\":\\\"Allow\\\",\\\"Principal\\\":{\\\"AWS\\\":\\\"arn:aws:iam::239541129941:role/stackgen-bastion\\\"},\\\"Action\\\":\\\"sts:AssumeRole\\\",\\\"Condition\\\":{\\\"StringEquals\\\":{\\\"sts:ExternalId\\\":\\\"cSdmUK8jn7\\\"}}},{\\\"Effect\\\":\\\"Allow\\\",\\\"Principal\\\":{\\\"AWS\\\":\\\"arn:aws:iam::239541129941:role/stackgen-bastion\\\"},\\\"Action\\\":\\\"sts:TagSession\\\"}]}\" \u0026\u0026 aws iam attach-role-policy --role-name \"$ROLE\" --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/ReadOnlyAccess \u0026\u0026 aws iam get-role --role-name \"$ROLE\" --query 'Role.Arn' --output text","org_id":"c8e8f44b-c501-4f55-b2f9-5677fbf2b43e","trust_policy":"{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Principal\": {\n        \"AWS\": \"arn:aws:iam::239541129941:role/stackgen-bastion\"\n      },\n      \"Action\": \"sts:AssumeRole\",\n      \"Condition\": {\n        \"StringEquals\": {\n          \"sts:ExternalId\": \"cSdmUK8jn7\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Principal\": {\n        \"AWS\": \"arn:aws:iam::239541129941:role/stackgen-bastion\"\n      },\n      \"Action\": \"sts:TagSession\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"},"sensitive_attributes":[]}]},{"module":"module.aws_iam[0]","mode":"managed","type":"aws_iam_role","name":"integration","provider":"provider[\"registry.opentofu.org/hashicorp/aws\"]","instances":[{"schema_version":0,"attributes":{"arn":"arn:aws:iam::339712749745:role/stackgen-aios-readonly","assume_role_policy":"{\"Statement\":[{\"Action\":\"sts:AssumeRole\",\"Condition\":{\"StringEquals\":{\"sts:ExternalId\":\"cSdmUK8jn7\"}},\"Effect\":\"Allow\",\"Principal\":{\"AWS\":\"arn:aws:iam::239541129941:role/stackgen-bastion\"}},{\"Action\":\"sts:TagSession\",\"Effect\":\"Allow\",\"Principal\":{\"AWS\":\"arn:aws:iam::239541129941:role/stackgen-bastion\"}}],\"Version\":\"2012-10-17\"}","create_date":"2026-06-17T17:41:51Z","description":"","force_detach_policies":false,"id":"stackgen-aios-readonly","inline_policy":[],"managed_policy_arns":[],"max_session_duration":3600,"name":"stackgen-aios-readonly","name_prefix":"","path":"/","permissions_boundary":"","tags":null,"tags_all":{},"unique_id":"AROAU6GDVGCYYIVMVGMEF"},"sensitive_attributes":[],"private":"bnVsbA==","dependencies":["data.sg_vault_aws_config.workspace"],"identity":{"account_id":"339712749745","name":"stackgen-aios-readonly"},"identity_schema_version":0}]},{"module":"module.aws_iam[0]","mode":"managed","type":"aws_iam_role_policy_attachment","name":"managed","provider":"provider[\"registry.opentofu.org/hashicorp/aws\"]","instances":[{"index_key":"arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/ReadOnlyAccess","schema_version":0,"attributes":{"id":"stackgen-aios-readonly/arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/ReadOnlyAccess","policy_arn":"arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/ReadOnlyAccess","role":"stackgen-aios-readonly"},"sensitive_attributes":[],"private":"bnVsbA==","dependencies":["data.sg_vault_aws_config.workspace","module.aws_iam.aws_iam_role.integration"],"identity":{"account_id":"339712749745","policy_arn":"arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/ReadOnlyAccess","role":"stackgen-aios-readonly"},"identity_schema_version":0}]},{"module":"module.aws_integration","mode":"managed","type":"terraform_data","name":"validate_secret_input","provider":"provider[\"terraform.io/builtin/terraform\"]","instances":[{"schema_version":0,"attributes":{"id":"790a6b29-b1fb-d1d3-c9cc-5d012b9067d6","input":null,"output":null,"triggers_replace":null},"sensitive_attributes":[],"dependencies":["data.sg_vault_aws_config.workspace","module.aws_iam.aws_iam_role.integration"]}]},{"module":"module.github_integration","mode":"managed","type":"sg_guild_integration","name":"github","provider":"provider[\"releases.stackgen.com/stackgen/stackgen\"]","instances":[{"schema_version":0,"attributes":{"credential_provider_id":null,"description":"GitHub SCM integration for repository operations, PRs, and code analysis","enabled":true,"env":{},"id":"1b46c085-9e86-5793-8cf1-1b7c86c05954","image":{"name":"ghcr.io/appcd-dev/stackgen-guild-integration-github:main","registry_credentials_secret":null},"name":"sre-boost-github","scope":"PROJECT","secret_ref_ids":["157aeb38-f196-554c-a34e-8a0478207c37"],"type":"github"},"sensitive_attributes":[[{"type":"get_attr","value":"secret_ref_ids"}],[{"type":"get_attr","value":"secret_ref_ids"},{"type":"index","value":{"value":0,"type":"number"}}]],"dependencies":["module.github_integration.sg_secret.github_vault"]}]},{"module":"module.github_integration","mode":"managed","type":"sg_secret","name":"github_vault","provider":"provider[\"releases.stackgen.com/stackgen/stackgen\"]","instances":[{"index_key":0,"schema_version":0,"attributes":{"category":"SCM","created_at":"2026-06-17 17:33:32.053578 +0000 UTC","description":"GitHub personal access token for SCM integration","id":"157aeb38-f196-554c-a34e-8a0478207c37","metadata":{"provider":"github","token":"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"},"name":"sre-boost-github-vault","org_id":null,"owner":"c8e8f44b-c501-4f55-b2f9-5677fbf2b43e","owner_type":"Organization","share_with_tenant":false,"shared_with":null,"subcategory":"github","updated_at":"2026-06-17 17:33:32.053578 +0000 UTC"},"sensitive_attributes":[[{"type":"get_attr","value":"metadata"},{"type":"index","value":{"value":"token","type":"string"}}]]}]},{"module":"module.github_integration","mode":"managed","type":"terraform_data","name":"validate_secret_input","provider":"provider[\"terraform.io/builtin/terraform\"]","instances":[{"schema_version":0,"attributes":{"id":"23667b67-8e07-7e61-b1b5-fbbd0aaac953","input":null,"output":null,"triggers_replace":null},"sensitive_attributes":[]}]},{"module":"module.remote_runner","mode":"managed","type":"sg_remote_runner","name":"this","provider":"provider[\"releases.stackgen.com/stackgen/stackgen\"]","instances":[{"index_key":0,"schema_version":0,"attributes":{"attached_agents":null,"capabilities":null,"cli_start_command":"aiden-runner start --runner-token sg_aios_4fea4f58-091f-4da8-b615-71d63c61c6c8 --mothership https://ai.dev.stackgen.com --auto-discover","description